# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# The Expo app lives at the repo root, but three unrelated deployables sit
# beneath it — backend/, web/ and admin/, each with its own node_modules. EAS
# tars the project directory and uploads it, so without this file every cloud
# build ships a Node API, two Next.js apps and their dependency trees to a
# machine that will never run them. That is slow, expensive, and puts server
# code (including .env files, if one were ever committed) into a build context
# that has no use for it.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for upload purposes when present, so the
# node_modules/build-output rules from .gitignore have to be restated here.

# ── Other deployables — never part of the mobile build ──
backend/
web/
admin/

# ── Dependencies and build output ──
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.next/

# ── Local infrastructure ──
docker-compose.yml
Makefile
start-all.sh
start-all.cmd
stop-all.sh
stop-all.cmd
.logs/
.github/

# ── Docs ──
docs/
*.md

# ── Design and marketing art that no screen requires ──
# assetBundlePatterns already keeps these out of the app bundle; this keeps them
# out of the upload too (about.png and sawa.png are ~2 MB each).
assets/about.png
assets/sawa.png
assets/sawa-icon.png
assets/refference.png

# ── Secrets and signing material — belt and braces ──
.env
.env.*
*.p8
*.p12
*.keystore
*-service-account.json
